  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="Tag574" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;General&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Description of Business&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 4.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Valero Partners Lucas, LLC (the &amp;#8220;Company&amp;#8221;) is a Delaware limited liability corporation and an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of Valero Energy Corporation (&amp;#8220;Valero&amp;#8221;). The Company&amp;#8217;s crude pipelines and terminalling assets are located in Jefferson County, Texas, and supply the Valero Port Arthur Refinery. Crude oil is received into the Company&amp;#8217;s pipelines and terminal from the Sunoco Logistics Nederland and Enterprise Beaumont marine terminals and the Seaway, Cameron Highway, and TC Energy Cushing MarketLink pipelines.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 4.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 107%;"&gt;The Company did not have any significant changes in operations during the year.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;em style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The Company is subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;#8220;FERC&amp;#8221;). These financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;em style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Participation in a Cash Management Program&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The Company reports a zero cash balance due to participation in a cash management program. Cash management or "money pool" programs typically concentrate affiliates' cash asset in joint accounts for the purpose of providing financial flexibility and lowering the cost of borrowing.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;In accordance with FERC Order 634-A, 68 FR 62004, dated October 31, 2003, as amended at 69 FR 9045, dated February 26, 2004, a Cash Management Agreement has been filed with FERC.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;em style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Property and Equipment&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The cost of property and equipment purchased or constructed, including betterments of property and equipment, is capitalized at historical cost. However, the cost of repairs to and normal maintenance of property and equipment is expensed when incurred. Betterments of property and equipment are those that extend the useful lives of the property and equipment or improve the safety of operations. The cost of property and equipment constructed includes interest and certain overhead costs allocable to construction activities. Interest capitalized during construction is included in the underlying accounts charged with the cost of the property to which such interest is related.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;When property and equipment are retired or replaced, the cost and related accumulated depreciation are eliminated, with any gain or loss reflected in depreciation expense, unless such amounts are reported separately due to materiality.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The Company computes depreciation using rates filed with and approved by FERC. Depreciation by carrier property account is provided on Pages 216-217 of this filing.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;em style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Employee Benefits&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The Company does not have any employees, and all of the personnel that conduct the Company&amp;#8217;s business are employed by an affiliate of Valero. Valero, through its affiliate, is responsible for compensating these personnel and sponsors certain postretirement benefit plans. All assets and liabilities associated with these plans are carried by Valero&amp;#8217;s affiliate.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The employee benefit expenses in the statement of income represent the cost that would have resulted if the Company were a stand-alone entity. Accordingly, the calculations of these expenses require certain assumptions, allocations and estimates which management believes are reasonable to represent the cost to the Company as a stand-alone entity. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top: 6.0pt;"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;em style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The Company is a single-member limited liability company and was structured as a disregarded entity for federal and state income tax purposes. Accordingly, no provision for income taxes is made in the Company&amp;#8217;s financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Other&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;em style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The Company did not have any significant commitments or contingencies at year end.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;em style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Rate or Regulatory Matters&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The Company was not directly involved in any significant rate or regulatory matters during the year.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
